1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,477
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,040
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,800
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,457
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting?

11
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,377
Either way, I'm feeling alive!

12
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,797
Look out below.

13
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,080
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,397
Raise your flag up high!

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,040
Hail a brand new dawn!

16
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,837
Blaze across the sky!

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,837
Time to journey on!

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,317
On your mark!

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,217
Camel of other things!

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,300
We're on Earth, a legendary!

21
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,620
If you can show your breath,
then we'll make some waves!

22
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:01,617
We run our daunted, ain't no beginners!

23
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,357
Cause if you're wanted,
then you're a winner!

24
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,840
For we are on the cruise,
and freedom is the only rule!

25
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:14,180
Fearless night and day,
cause that's just our way!

26
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,537
Find one piece, I'll be the first!

27
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,437
I'll put it, be so bad, so good first!

28
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,137
It's all this real!

29
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,257
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel!

30
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:29,457
I'm done playing, feel it's waiting!

31
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:31,457
In a world I'm feeling alive!

32
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,237
But I'll be loud!

33
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:37,040
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

34
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far!

35
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:44,320
Gotta make it to the end!

36
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,337
Whatever danger we find!

37
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:47,677
No one ever left behind!

38
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,760
I've always got your back, my friend!

39
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward!

40
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,117
Dreaming from the very
first day I'd make my name!

41
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,200
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed!

42
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave!

43
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,640
In the world I'm feeling
alive, look out below!

44
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:13,080
Wake up, sunshine!

45
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:17,140
Wake up, sunshine!

46
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,177
Wake up, sunshine!

47
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:23,660
And here we go!

48
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,320
We go!

49
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,430
No!

50
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:35,180
You're staying right here!

51
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,070
Don't fight.

52
00:02:37,153 --> 00:02:37,983
It's pointless.

53
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:39,210
Come on.

54
00:02:39,293 --> 00:02:41,620
We're just wasting time. Yes, right.

55
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:44,234
If we don't hurry, they'll kill father.

56
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,968
I already told you, Jinbei!

57
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:49,037
Get out of my way so I can go
and kick this horny guy's ass!

58
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,780
And I told you to wait!

59
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,597
You aren't listening at all!

60
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,033
Let me finish speaking!

61
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:57,597
Now, how would you describe
the relationship between us?

62
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,510
We're friends!

63
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,470
That's right.

64
00:03:00,553 --> 00:03:02,417
Although it is a simple matter for us,

65
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,017
our two peoples have been struggling to

66
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,806
establish such a
relationship for decades now.

67
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:10,040
I left you a message
saying not to fight Heart,

68
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:12,917
because I didn't want you
facing him recklessly.

69
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,040
Don't you see?

70
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,857
Think of how the fishman will view you.

71
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,597
If you rush in and show
aggression towards Carrot,

72
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:23,917
you'll be viewed as nothing more than just
another human bully oppressing our kind.

73
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,471
That is not what we want.

74
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,500
No, you should be a hero.

75
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,660
One that saves the island.

76
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,790
Hero?

77
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,820
Hell no! But why?

78
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,900
Obviously, because we're pirates! Come on!

79
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,660
Heroes are great, but I'm not one!

80
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:43,274
Seriously, do you even know
what you're asking me to do?

81
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:46,072
Let's say there's a chunk of meat, right?

82
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,717
Pirates will have a
banquet and dig right in,

83
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:52,317
but a hero would give it to other
people instead of eating it.

84
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,230
Screw that!

85
00:03:53,313 --> 00:03:54,161
My meat is mine!

86
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,440
What a reason.

87
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,397
Luffy, I'll let you have
all the meat you want.

88
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,560
Just do as I say.

89
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,190
That's fair.

90
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,140
No way!

91
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:04,817
I'll make this simple.

92
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:07,077
There will come a time
when I need your help

93
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:09,689
so you'll rush in when
that moment arrives.

94
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:10,710
Okay.

95
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:12,310
Good.

96
00:04:12,393 --> 00:04:13,360
But first, the plan.

97
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:15,260
We'll get caught on purpose.

98
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:22,040
To get us close afterwards while their
attention's on me then one of you pirates

99
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,217
will sneak out of megalo's
stomach and get yourself

100
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,257
into position to make
your attack did you see

101
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:34,537
a stomach the celestial

102
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,637
dragon's letter they have

103
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:41,420
it we need it hold on
what's this letter jimba?

104
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:45,234
Remember, Luffy was sleeping
through most of your story.

105
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:46,441
He doesn't know.

106
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,460
In short,

107
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:53,841
the letter is something Queen Otohime
acquired ten years ago at great personal risk.

108
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:56,726
It will define the very
future of this island.

109
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,737
They'll also have the key we'll need
to release the king from his bonds.

110
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,157
One of your crewmates must retrieve them.

111
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:05,237
Which one of you is up to the task?

112
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:09,496
I'm pretty good at stealing, but
still, I think I'll need Robin's help.

113
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,640
Of course.

114
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:12,410
Good.

115
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,157
Once you've managed to
free the king, get out.

116
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,358
I'll call Luffy and we'll take over.

117
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,377
After you emerge from Megalo's body,

118
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:22,497
the people of Fishman Island
will understand your intent.

119
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:26,698
Because they'll see you and I working
together against the common foe.

120
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:31,180
Princess, I must ask that you stay
somewhere safe outside the plaza.

121
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,217
It's for the best.

122
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:36,712
We'll pass the letter to you, whereupon
the entire royal family can escape.

123
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,360
During this time,

124
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:43,521
the rest of you will have to head to Ryugu
Palace to rescue your imprisoned friends.

125
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:48,020
Once they're free, get to the plaza
to back us up as soon as possible.

126
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:55,360
As for how you go about saving them, well,
that's for you to deal with. Come on!

127
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:56,410
Be specific!

128
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,990
Wow!

129
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,806
You can count on us big time!

130
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,335
After all, we've got the Sonny, right?

131
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,920
So no worries, we'll be there.

132
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:12,077
Once this is set in motion there's
no turning back we must succeed you

133
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:17,777
everyone here respects Jimbae whether
they're a civilian or outlaw they'll

134
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:22,857
follow after his example that's right
So if they see Jimbae working with

135
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:27,380
a human even a pirate they'll cheer
you on or maybe even fight beside you.

136
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,100
I mean, it's possible.

137
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,650
Strong hand.

138
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:33,740
Please, Luffy.

139
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,897
I'm only doing this
because you asked me to.

140
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:40,500
Got that? I made it.

141
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,960
Having people cheer for me? No thanks.

142
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,280
I don't like it.

143
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:47,237
I'm more for taking their
money and running away.

144
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,197
Speak for yourselves.

145
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:52,557
I'd go to the depths of hell if I knew the
mermaids would be there to cheer me on.

146
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:53,680
Very well, then.

147
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,597
Sounds like everything is settled, then.

148
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,080
All right, let's do this thing.

149
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,170
Wait.

150
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,980
Yeah, what's up? Something wrong?

151
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:07,940
What's our codename? Are
you kidding? Who cares?

152
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:09,800
We'll go already.

153
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,820
That's Skrya Luffy.

154
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,780
He's human and a pirate.

155
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,160
But on our side.

156
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:18,777
He showed up right when Princess
Shirahoshi called for him.

157
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:19,977
From the looks of things,

158
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:23,517
he's here to help Boss Team Bay
save the country from Horty's men.

159
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,620
Stop it!

160
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,976
Isn't it sweet how they cling to you?

161
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,238
But you've only delayed the
king's inevitable demise!

162
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,300
After all, you are nothing but a human!

163
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:39,040
Your beauty outshines
all others, princess!

164
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:45,377
Now that we've met, would you be
willing to show me your panties?

165
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,720
You can't ask her that!

166
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,340
Then show me yours!

167
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,980
No way in hell!

168
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,877
Okay, we're back!

169
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:56,860
Well done.

170
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,571
They're all ignoring you.

171
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,984
That's just because I was
using my inside voice.

172
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,240
Mommy Swan!

173
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:08,360
Now that I've saved those idiots from
the palace, you have to love me. Right?

174
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,470
Whatever.

175
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:12,220
Wait. He did what? Liar?

176
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,086
We got to the exit ourselves.

177
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:15,890
Maybe.

178
00:08:15,973 --> 00:08:20,780
However, you never would have escaped
without me. That's a joke. Right, you guys?

179
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:25,810
Shirahoshi.

180
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,833
It's your mom's letter.

181
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:28,870
Here you go.

182
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:31,989
I can't tell you how
much this means to me.

183
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:36,906
I know it may look like an ordinary piece
of paper, but it's this island's hope.

184
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:38,920
That's enough, Whip Hachi.

185
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,240
It's not safe.

186
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,280
He's right.

187
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:45,217
You weren't meant to be
caught, so you must leave.

188
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:46,840
Now, while you can.

189
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:48,920
Wait, Luffy.

190
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,900
What did you call me?

191
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,470
Huh?

192
00:08:52,553 --> 00:08:54,537
Just now, it was almost...

193
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:55,857
my name, but...

194
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:58,120
Yeah, I was wrong about you.

195
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:01,008
You're a wuss, but more
than just a crybaby.

196
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:03,240
So I'll call you Weepy Hachi.

197
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,040
It's an upgrade.

198
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:08,657
When a person feels as if
they've been wronged, well,

199
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:11,799
then it's only natural that
they would turn to hate.

200
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,940
That man.

201
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,630
Heart.

202
00:09:15,713 --> 00:09:17,100
He's doing exactly that.

203
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:20,660
But you chose not to hate.

204
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:23,160
A coward wouldn't do that.

205
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:26,300
Hardship has only made
you stronger in the end.

206
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,340
Nami is right.

207
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:29,977
You endured.

208
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:32,300
Princess, I'm proud of you.

209
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:34,980
I appreciate the thought, but still,

210
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:39,396
I feel like I caused everyone trouble
by keeping this secret to myself.

211
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:40,690
I'm sorry.

212
00:09:40,773 --> 00:09:41,640
You're mistaken.

213
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,057
You've done quite well.

214
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:48,077
Your intentions were pure, just
like those who have come before you.

215
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:52,337
You can't tell them
you have to hold it in.

216
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:57,037
Listen, don't become angry on my behalf!

217
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,877
I don't want that.

218
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:05,137
Our heroes planted a seed in your
heart and it has blossomed beautifully.

219
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:07,177
You have lived by their example.

220
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:10,577
Well, if everyone else
thought the way you do,

221
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:14,017
then there would be no
more fighting and the

222
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:16,217
conflict between fishmen
and humans would be?

223
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,320
over at last.

224
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:22,152
You may have suffered through those
past years alone, but that doesn't make

225
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:23,917
that time meaningless.

226
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:28,020
Single-handedly, you are a
defender, protecting the virtues of

227
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,537
others day after day.

228
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:32,480
But today, we're here.

229
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:34,440
We'll protect them for you.

230
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,757
I killed

231
00:10:55,840 --> 00:11:02,420
so much!

232
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,560
You still cry, baby.

233
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:08,900
That's for sure.

234
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:11,210
Strahd!

235
00:11:11,293 --> 00:11:12,123
Take him down!

236
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:19,260
I should have known Vander
Decken was going to fail me.

237
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:22,385
He couldn't even get rid
of one lousy princess.

238
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,400
Captain Heart!

239
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:36,480
Her power is too great.

240
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,860
It really is the stuff of legends.

241
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:44,560
Once I found out it was real I knew I had
to eliminate her as soon as possible. Sir.

242
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,680
But then, you got in my way.

243
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:50,710
Admittedly,

244
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:53,057
I should have known
something was wrong when

245
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:55,317
you were captured without
putting up a fight,

246
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,230
Jinbei.

247
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:01,000
You really like these humans, don't you?

248
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:03,177
People like you are the worst.

249
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,537
You've completely forgotten your pride.

250
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:08,208
See, you grew up with
Dock in our district.

251
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,087
And let's not forget Arlong.

252
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,920
He was like your brother.

253
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:14,537
Both of them were beaten
or killed by humans.

254
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:18,960
But instead of avenging them, you
wouldn't get in bed with the humans.

255
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,360
It's pathetic.

256
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,026
Jinbei, godless like Neptune.

257
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:26,337
But soon, everything is going to change.

258
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:28,640
Once I'm king, that is. Hear that?

259
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,781
I'll start with the world summit.

260
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:32,686
That'll be the perfect place.

261
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:37,691
With every ruler in the surface world
in one place, they'll be easy to kill.

262
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:42,140
Then the whole world will learn
to fear our underwater kingdom.

263
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,157
Their kingdoms in disarray
will drag the humans

264
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,769
into the depths and
enslave every last one.

265
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:54,117
In time, there won't be a
soul left to stand against us,

266
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,680
and we will rule the Great Pirate Era.

267
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:03,920
Oh yes, you pirates, we'll bow
the same as everybody else.

268
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,320
Just you wait. See?

269
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:11,424
These humans are more than capable of
holding their own, yet they kneel before me.

270
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,050
That's right.

271
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:15,356
In a moment you'll be just like them.

272
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:16,580
Straw Hats.

273
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:24,140
Is that so?

274
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:29,940
And to think there are only ten
of you here to stand in my way!

275
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:34,660
What can you possibly
do when we're 100,000?!

276
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:38,400
KILL THEM, NEW FISHMENT PIRATES!

277
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:42,480
Here they come!

278
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,155
No way we can fight this many at once!

279
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,380
We're done for!

280
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:50,662
This is exactly the reason I don't
like hanging out with you guys!

281
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:54,777
Before this begins, it's been a
pleasure traveling with all of you.

282
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:55,820
Don't say that!

283
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:58,220
There are so many enemies.

284
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:02,237
Wow, if I try to count them
all, my eyes may pop out.

285
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,340
And again, I don't have eyes.

286
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,880
So they can't!

287
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:08,400
Just 100,000?

288
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,875
That's nothing we can't handle, right?

289
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,220
Hey, wait!

290
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:15,734
You're just saying that because
you're hiding behind us!

291
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,280
And here I go!

292
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:18,680
It's time to shine!

293
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,260
Super Harbored Me! All right!

294
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,700
Let's do this already! Get over here!

295
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,500
In case you can't count,

296
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:31,637
we're each gonna have to take down
10,000 of these guys to win this fight.

297
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:34,838
They have numbers, but it
doesn't make them stronger.

298
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:38,057
I mean, it's not like they're
Navy Admirals or anything.

299
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:39,493
So don't crap yourself.

300
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,685
After these guys, you're next.

301
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:44,360
Number 10,001. Bring it on.

302
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,820
I can't wait.

303
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:50,780
Hey, Luffy.

304
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,400
Oh, no.

305
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,440
Those four million berries are mine.

306
00:14:58,720 --> 00:14:59,780
Now they're mine.

307
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:01,580
It's too easy.

308
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:04,680
Kill him!

309
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:40,950
Ah!

310
00:15:41,033 --> 00:15:42,567
What the hell just happened?

311
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:02,377
but he didn't do anything
and he still knocked them all

312
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:07,637
out hey get up guys come on
damn he took down half of us

313
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:11,697
in an instant that was 50 000
of our men what did he even

314
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:17,217
do did everyone see that yeah
but i don't know what it was

315
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:21,837
so much power for one so young
wait did the Straw Hat guy

316
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:27,877
really do that yeah too cool
that Haki that training paid

317
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:34,277
off i see unreal i mean
conqueror's Haki scary sure is

318
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,772
but i'd expect no less otherwise
he couldn't be my captain

319
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:42,020
Your name's Heart, right?

320
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,360
I'm about to kick your ass.

321
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:47,677
You want to become the king
of a country or whatever?

322
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:48,900
Fine, I don't care.

323
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:53,480
But king of the pirates? Nuh-uh.

324
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:54,940
That's my job.

325
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:57,080
It's true.

326
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,940
We may have lost 50,000.

327
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,240
But take heart.

328
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:05,600
We still have 50,000 left.

329
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:14,097
Those insufferable Straw Hat Pirates have
sought to shadow our dreams at every turn.

330
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,560
They must pay!

331
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:26,220
The traitor Jinbei is no better.

332
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:30,260
He follows in Otohime's footsteps
and befriends the humans.

333
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:34,140
But that is not the future
we fishmen wish to create!

334
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,550
He's right!

335
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:36,997
Straw Hat's a damn human!

336
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:39,617
What the hell does he
know about our people?

337
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:40,530
Anjibe!

338
00:17:40,613 --> 00:17:43,991
If he wants to turn his back
on his brothers, kill him too!

339
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,844
Geez, you knocked out too many.

340
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:58,040
Leave some for me. Oh, yeah. My bad.

341
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:00,861
Hey, don't get ahead of yourself.

342
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:03,020
I'm taking 30,000.

343
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,777
Got it, lost head?

344
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:07,020
Shut up, dirty cook.

345
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:12,340
You're dead now!

346
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:14,180
Don't mess with us!

347
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,420
Okay!

348
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:25,520
Go third gear!

349
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:30,480
Just come at me!

350
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,100
I'll take all of you!

351
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:40,420
His arm is I know it's huge here goes.

352
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:50,840
Quick we had better assist him!

353
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:59,360
This is heaven for me I
won't let you destroy it.

354
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:04,917
Still don't want to give
up well more fun for

355
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,597
me I was thinking this
island is teeming with.

356
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:13,877
Invaluable archaeological resources the way
you're rampaging around and damaging it.

357
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:18,217
You ought to be ashamed look at

358
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:21,580
that crown they're ready to rock.

359
00:19:24,060 --> 00:19:29,240
I'd say a 50,000-man brawl is the perfect
time to take them for a test drive.

360
00:19:29,620 --> 00:19:30,450
Test drive?

361
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,500
Did you say them? Them who?

362
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:36,100
The Sonny just got two
brand-new weapons. Big ones.

363
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:38,086
Do you guys want to see them?

364
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:40,300
Yeah, of course we do!

365
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,893
You should keep an eye on your princess.

366
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,180
That's a pretty big target.

367
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,357
She's mine now!

368
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,060
The Water Shot!

369
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:10,200
They didn't need me after all.

370
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,777
Did you see that crap?

371
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:21,625
He deflected Captain Horty's water shot
with his own, like it was nothing at all!

372
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:24,153
I am so done with that big blue traitor!

373
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:27,320
He's as much trouble as
Straw Hats, maybe more!

374
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:31,180
Huh, that raw power of yours
is harnessed very poorly.

375
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,940
Your fishman karate needs work.

376
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:37,602
Wait a minute, I've heard
stories about this guy.

377
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:40,417
He was the first fishman
to join the Seven Warlords.

378
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,197
Yeah, and then after he resigned,

379
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,280
his bounty jumped up to
400 million berries, right?

380
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,460
This is hopeless.

381
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:48,625
We can't win against that guy.

382
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,417
Why don't you fools stop
chattering and start fighting?

383
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:56,337
If you intend to kill the princess, you'll
have to square with the rest of us first.

384
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,840
Go forward, Iron Shell Squad.

385
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:04,540
Three swords time.

386
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:14,720
Black Rope.

387
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:16,390
Shotsumaki!

388
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,580
Ah, he cut through their shells.

389
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,857
It's like they were made out of cheese.

390
00:21:28,940 --> 00:21:29,920
What the hell?

391
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,591
They all drop like flies.

392
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:33,918
Is this guy the Grim Reaper or what?

393
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:35,520
It's not doing work.

394
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,620
This is sick.

395
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,300
It's a sword hurricane.

396
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,520
Ryan, you're gonna get cut.

397
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:45,660
How long is this thing gonna last?

398
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:48,820
...until you get to hell.

399
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:53,880
Why don't you idiots use your brains?

400
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,215
Inflate your bubbles!

401
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:57,600
Let's go!

402
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:00,980
Attack from the sky!

403
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:03,260
Kill Pichiro Hachi!

404
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,640
Watch out, we'll stab you!

405
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,160
Go, Harrison Bond!

406
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:12,340
It's the Sea Urchin Spike Unit!

407
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,405
And the leader, Harrison Bond!

408
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:19,400
Before you do anything else,
take out the kicking guy!

409
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:21,710
Harry...

410
00:22:21,793 --> 00:22:22,720
Seth... Paul!

411
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,600
Well, what are you gonna do now, huh?

412
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,350
Sanji!

413
00:22:28,433 --> 00:22:29,300
Do be careful!

414
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:33,320
How can you be so calm
at a time like this? Hey!

415
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:43,260
It's been a while since then.

416
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,817
I ran like hell.

417
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:53,337
Come back candy boy!

418
00:22:53,420 --> 00:22:55,017
Over my dead body.

419
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:58,557
I brought my favorite dress just for you.

420
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:00,957
Why don't you try it all?

421
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:03,077
Don't be shy, it's just us.

422
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:05,900
That's not the problem, forget it.

423
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,977
Through the rain.

424
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:10,780
And the snow.

425
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:17,340
Through thunder and
lightning, I never stopped.

426
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:23,320
Cigar fires, you stubborn bastard!

427
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,380
Aren't you adorable?

428
00:23:25,860 --> 00:23:28,157
You can't just run away
from us forever, you know?

429
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,857
One of these days, we're starting
to catch right up to you!

430
00:23:30,940 --> 00:23:32,100
Oh, Sanji

431
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:36,788
I've gotten myself out of tougher
spots than this, haven't I?

432
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:38,890
Sanji!

433
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:44,559
My courage had left me and
there was nowhere to run.

434
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,750
Then...

435
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:06,780
What the? He's gone!

436
00:24:13,780 --> 00:24:15,920
I found a new path.

437
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:23,780
And then before long I.

438
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,500
Was flying!

439
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,060
Skywalk?

440
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:43,880
Sanji can walk on air now,
like those other guys!

441
00:24:51,540 --> 00:24:53,160
Skywalk. Oh, I see.

442
00:24:53,580 --> 00:24:54,660
Not moonwalk.

443
00:24:56,660 --> 00:24:57,780
Hey, scumbags!

444
00:24:58,300 --> 00:24:59,130
Whoa!

445
00:24:59,380 --> 00:25:00,360
He's flying!

446
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:04,877
If you've got something to say to the
princess, she'll have to go through me first.

447
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:06,980
Because I just happen to be her.

448
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,860
Knight in shining armor!

449
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:10,480
Thank you, Sanji.

450
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:12,820
Are you some kind of wise guy?

451
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:17,000
Let's cook these small fries.

452
00:25:29,100 --> 00:25:31,260
Let's get this over with already!

453
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:42,557
Actually, I have a better idea!

454
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:47,337
How about instead, we leave the world's
most lovely mermaid princess alone, huh?!

455
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,380
Now here's some party music!

456
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,020
What's going on?

457
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:55,880
Why'd it get dark?

458
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:02,140
Welcome all to this festival night!

459
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:04,200
What the...

460
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:21,180
I guess, it was not a dream,
that big fight we were having.

461
00:26:21,540 --> 00:26:24,740
Now, it's time to set up the fireworks!

462
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:34,720
I mean, this is much fun in years! Ha-ha!

463
00:26:41,580 --> 00:26:42,580
It's beautiful!

464
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:45,877
Hey, what the hell are you guys aiming at?

465
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:46,790
Just kill her!

466
00:26:47,280 --> 00:26:49,460
Yeah, but we can't.

467
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,557
We're enjoying the festival too much.

468
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:52,470
Cut.

469
00:26:52,553 --> 00:26:53,700
Sorry, party's over.

470
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,620
Queen Tortillas, Fantasia.

471
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,020
Neal, move!

472
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:13,080
Gigantesco, mono!

473
00:27:15,820 --> 00:27:16,720
Legs!

474
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,100
And stop!

475
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,640
Sorry!

476
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:30,657
There's a lot of screaming going on.

477
00:27:30,740 --> 00:27:31,916
Is that good or bad?

478
00:27:32,260 --> 00:27:34,757
It's way too cramped for
us all to be in here.

479
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:36,217
Then why don't you get out?

480
00:27:36,300 --> 00:27:38,337
You're not even interested
in the weapons anyway.

481
00:27:38,420 --> 00:27:40,477
Because if I go outside,
I'm going to have to fight.

482
00:27:40,560 --> 00:27:42,697
I don't want to be stuck out there either.

483
00:27:42,780 --> 00:27:45,545
Franky, can we hurry
this up a little, please?

484
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:52,400
I can't rush greatness, kid.

485
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:59,320
But fine, let's do this.

486
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:04,537
Actually, I'm getting
pretty excited now, too!

487
00:28:04,620 --> 00:28:06,217
That's great, but can you move?

488
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:08,300
I'm supposed to operate this thing

489
00:28:12,060 --> 00:28:13,760
It got bigger

490
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:16,760
Why couldn't it start out this way?

491
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,077
It's showtime!

492
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:22,800
There ain't nothin'
stoppin' this unveiling!

493
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,230
Wait, wait!

494
00:28:24,313 --> 00:28:25,143
Yeah, but for what?

495
00:28:25,460 --> 00:28:26,820
Let's rock and roll!

496
00:28:34,580 --> 00:28:36,400
Get him swatted in there!

497
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:41,960
It doesn't matter how big
your legs or arms are,

498
00:28:42,180 --> 00:28:46,437
cause you ain't gonna be nothin' but a
dead woman once we get our sneakers in ya!

499
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:47,880
Better than that case!

500
00:28:56,300 --> 00:28:58,697
Soldier Dark Sister.

501
00:28:58,780 --> 00:29:01,520
Channel 4.

502
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:09,240
Arch Black Rhino.

503
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:19,200
It's F R U 4.

504
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:40,617
A motorbike! So cool! I want it!

505
00:29:40,700 --> 00:29:42,171
That's one tough machine!

506
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:43,261
And stylish too!

507
00:29:43,760 --> 00:29:45,600
Let's see this venom of yours!

508
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,480
He's coming right at us!

509
00:29:51,580 --> 00:29:54,286
You can try stinging it
if you really want to!

510
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,860
But this monster's made of pure steel!

511
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:04,640
How was that?

512
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:06,580
On a scale of one to super!

513
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,320
Someone stop that guy!

514
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:10,400
I got him!

515
00:30:10,660 --> 00:30:12,500
Time for steel on steel!

516
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:15,180
Just leave it to me, boys!

517
00:30:19,760 --> 00:30:20,590
Come on!

518
00:30:20,673 --> 00:30:22,208
You're not scared, are you?

519
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:50,780
The new number, Shadow 5!

520
00:30:52,980 --> 00:30:55,160
Brachiotek 5 is here!

521
00:30:58,480 --> 00:30:59,457
No way!

522
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:00,380
A dinosaur!

523
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:05,360
You guys see that perfect shot I made?

524
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:09,537
Yeah, but I don't think you're
using this to its full potential.

525
00:31:09,620 --> 00:31:12,738
Man, and here I thought
Brachio was just a shipwright.

526
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:16,660
Attention! Cock 2!

527
00:31:16,940 --> 00:31:18,340
I'm Commander Chopper!

528
00:31:18,620 --> 00:31:21,480
We have enemy bogeys
inbound off our 9 o 'clock!

529
00:31:39,940 --> 00:31:42,160
Hey, you need a fight, too!

530
00:31:45,760 --> 00:31:46,900
This is crazy.

531
00:31:47,260 --> 00:31:49,297
I mean, they didn't look this tough.

532
00:31:49,380 --> 00:31:50,657
There's only ten of them,

533
00:31:50,740 --> 00:31:54,740
but they're taking on a hundred
thousand like it was nothing at all.

534
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,460
We're counting on you!

535
00:31:57,700 --> 00:31:58,840
Get up, Timmy!

536
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:02,480
This has gone on too long.

537
00:32:06,540 --> 00:32:08,080
Rise! My Kraken!

538
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:35,950
Whoa!

539
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:37,020
It's huge!

540
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:41,440
You have ten targets.

541
00:32:41,660 --> 00:32:45,200
Kill the humans. Go!
Crush them! You heard me!

542
00:32:57,960 --> 00:33:00,597
It doesn't matter how
strong the Straw Hats are,

543
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:04,357
they're all goners if they get
smashed by those giant tentacles.

544
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:08,097
Yeah, the Kraken always does
whatever Captain Ordy tells it to do.

545
00:33:08,180 --> 00:33:09,700
And it's strong as hell!

546
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:14,113
They don't have a pair against
our deep-de-wrecking ball!

547
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:16,880
Oh, hey, it's that thing.

548
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:22,940
What are you waiting for?

549
00:33:24,760 --> 00:33:25,800
Get to it!

550
00:33:26,460 --> 00:33:30,177
Seeing as I'm the one who dragged you
here all the way from the North Pole,

551
00:33:30,260 --> 00:33:31,789
that makes me your master.

552
00:33:32,140 --> 00:33:33,620
So kill them already!

553
00:33:37,280 --> 00:33:38,720
Or I kill you.

554
00:33:55,300 --> 00:33:57,124
Please, can we talk about this?

555
00:34:00,860 --> 00:34:02,140
Oh, hey, Tsutome!

556
00:34:03,900 --> 00:34:06,312
Don't tell me you can't see me down here!

557
00:34:06,540 --> 00:34:08,187
You were my pet for a while!

558
00:34:08,580 --> 00:34:09,874
You and I are buddies!

559
00:34:14,180 --> 00:34:15,420
We found him!

560
00:34:15,900 --> 00:34:16,800
Luffy, no!

561
00:34:24,960 --> 00:34:25,800
That's people!

562
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:28,289
Hey, knock it off, cinema!

563
00:34:34,220 --> 00:34:35,050
Yeah!

564
00:34:35,380 --> 00:34:36,210
Alrighty!

565
00:34:36,293 --> 00:34:37,123
Alrighty!

566
00:34:37,206 --> 00:34:38,036
Let's get moving!

567
00:34:38,119 --> 00:34:38,949
Ha ha ha ha!

568
00:34:39,032 --> 00:34:39,862
Ha ha ha ha!

569
00:34:43,160 --> 00:34:43,990
Ah!

570
00:34:44,073 --> 00:34:45,920
The dragon has betrayed us!

571
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:52,710
Dragon!

572
00:34:52,793 --> 00:34:53,940
Knock it off!

573
00:34:54,580 --> 00:34:55,815
You're the occupants!

574
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:02,060
Crusher! All right!

575
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:05,900
Captain, help me.

576
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,220
Go that way, buddy!

577
00:35:10,500 --> 00:35:12,380
Dammit! What's going on?

578
00:35:12,640 --> 00:35:15,360
It's doing everything Straw Hat says!

579
00:35:15,620 --> 00:35:16,600
But why?

580
00:35:21,580 --> 00:35:22,980
Listen up, Tsurume!

581
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:26,124
I want you to stay here
and protect Weepy Hachi!

582
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:42,617
I can't believe you managed to
ingratiate yourself to the Kraken.

583
00:35:42,700 --> 00:35:47,217
It seems no matter where you go, you
always befriend the highest caliber allies.

584
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:48,130
Think so?

585
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:52,692
Um, thank you very much for
lending us your power, Sodom.

586
00:36:00,820 --> 00:36:03,114
There's still a lot of these guys left.

587
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:11,020
All right, bring it on.
